  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Fixes\n\nMembers named with escaped keywords (#363, closes #359). A member declared with an escaped keyword name, such as @class, @event or @object, was written bare in the imposter and failed to compile. Such names are now escaped wherever generated code uses them.\n\nSame-signature methods that differ only in allows ref struct (#365, closes #356). Two interfaces' methods with the same signature, where only one type parameter allows ref structs, got two implicit implementations (CS0111, CS0425). They're now implemented explicitly, like methods whose constraints differ in other ways.\n\nA type parameter named like the imposter class (#366, closes #354). A target such as IService\\<IServiceImposter> generated class IServiceImposter\\<IServiceImposter> (CS0694). The imposter keeps its name, and the type parameter takes another one in generated code.\n\nDocumentation\n\nMember types from other source generators (#367). A member whose type another source generator produces keeps working: the type is written through and binds in the final compilation, as long as it's referenced fully qualified. An event whose delegate type comes from another generator is left out of the imposter. Its workaround is documented, and regression tests cover both cases.\n\nMaintenance\n\nThe generator dropped some dead code and renamed a check (#360, #361). Generated output is unchanged.",
